{"kind":"request","text":"Review draft 1 of the design note for outside effects by a\npublisher member (request 35cbcb29, promise 885d9876) at\nffa498e2, branch `planner/publisher-member-20261113`, base main\n57e893c0.\n\nOne path: `notes/2026-11-13-publisher-member.md`, 421 lines.\n\nA design review session wrote draft 1 at Hugh's request (head\n759b3ce2). I took the note in promise 885d9876. The head adds a\nmerge of main and one commit of corrected facts (ffa498e2): the\nbase head, two line counts, the trailer's scope and genesis, the\n`repository-binding` cohort, the place of the GitHub App key, the\ntest support file, the roadmap heading, one quotation, and the\nsentence on `lending.publish`. An agent checked 55 source facts\nat 57e893c0, and I read each correction against source.\n\nWhat the note decides. A scope never sends to an outside system.\nA member with a publisher role writes to the Git host and signs\nan act that states the result. The record uses declared forms:\nfour slots and four acts on one item. Slice P1 publishes the\nshelf pages of the lending library in a room with host `none`,\nwith eight witnesses and no network.\n\nHugh has not ratified the note. Two decisions are his: who runs\na hosted publisher and holds its Git credential, and whether\nslice P1 is inside the stable base. I recommend P1 as a side lane\nafter CF-1 and the cutover deployment.\n\nAsked of the review:\n1. Architecture: the route, and the five questions of section 10\n   that the note leaves open.\n2. Security: the Git credential moves from the platform to a\n   member. A wrong or late `published` act, a revoked publisher,\n   and a lost answer.\n3. Kernel: section 8 states that P1 adds nothing to\n   `packages/contract`, `derive` or `bytes` and names no K item.\n   Confirm that reading.\n4. Simplification.\n\nChecks at the head: `check-doc-links` (1,245 links, 0 broken),\n`check-notes` (0 warnings), `check-commit-messages` (3 checked, 0\nflagged) and `git diff --check`. No